# Template drift allowlist for zudo-design-token-lint (doc site).
# Generated projects start from create-zudo-doc templates; this file lists
# intentional divergences so `pnpm check:template-drift` exits 0.
#
# Format: one repo-relative path per line (no leading slash).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# Re-baselined against create-zudo-doc 5.8.0 (the version pinned in
# doc/package.json's devDependencies) after the 4.x doc-site rescaffold
# (issue #150). The drift check (scripts/check-template-drift.sh) only walks
# node_modules/create-zudo-doc/templates/{base,features}; top-level identity
# files (zfb.config.ts, wrangler.toml, package.json, setup-preset.json) have
# no template counterpart there and are never compared, so they need no
# allowlist entry. The old pre-rescaffold entries (settings.ts/settings-types.ts,
# pages/lib/, per-feature component shims, etc.) are gone because the files
# and template feature dirs they referenced no longer exist in the 4.5.0
# template shape — nothing to allowlist for paths the drift check no longer
# walks at all.

# scripts/setup-doc-skill.sh is intentionally customized for this repo's
# hybrid layout. The template version assumes Claude/Codex resources live
# inside the doc-app itself (project root == doc/); this repo's `.claude/`
# lives one level ABOVE `doc/`, at the repo root (root = the npm lint
# package, doc/ = the doc site). The customized script resolves the project
# name from the ROOT package.json (not doc/package.json), reads/writes
# `.claude/skills/` at the repo root (never `doc/.claude`), and does not
# implement the template's newer --target/tracked-skill-linking machinery
# (single Claude Code target only; no Codex support needed here).
scripts/setup-doc-skill.sh

# pages/docs/[[...slug]].tsx and pages/[locale]/docs/[[...slug]].tsx replace
# the generated `virtual:zudo-doc-chrome-bindings` import with a STATIC
# relative import of src/chrome-bindings, because this site's docs use a
# custom <Playground> interactive island that the virtual-module (SSR-only)
# path can't make scanner-reachable. Both files carry an in-file comment
# explaining the substitution (zudo-doc's "Interactive islands
# (experimental)" recipe). Everything else is byte-identical to the template.
pages/docs/[[...slug]].tsx
pages/[locale]/docs/[[...slug]].tsx

# src/styles/global.css carries project-specific content beyond the
# generated @slot markers: brand typography overrides (Futura page titles/
# header logo, currently inert while themePack: "bauhaus" is active — see
# the in-file comment), extra `@source` content globs for src/components,
# and the designTokenPanel import. See the file's own header comments for
# the full rationale; not reproduced here to avoid a second copy drifting
# from the first.
src/styles/global.css

# The project uses branded generated favicon assets rather than the generic
# create-zudo-doc files. The SVG template is intentionally absent because the
# detailed source mark is unreadable at favicon sizes.
public/favicon-16x16.png
public/favicon-32x32.png
public/favicon.ico
public/favicon.svg

# This repo's link checker includes stricter versioned-route and allowlist
# behavior than the generic scaffolded checker.
scripts/check-links.js
